mk("AUTHORS","Author","Haruki Murakami","Japanese novelist who was watching a baseball game in 1978 when an American player hit a double and Murakami suddenly knew he could write a novel. He bought paper on the way home. His books mix cats, jazz, parallel worlds, and women who disappear. He ran a jazz bar in Tokyo before becoming a writer.","","Kafka on the Shore, first 3 chapters",30,"Read the opening chapters. Two narratives alternate: Kafka Tamura, a 15-year-old runaway, and Nakata, an old man who can talk to cats. Notice how Murakami describes surreal events with the same flat tone he uses for making spaghetti — the magic never announces itself. The cats are the most normal people in the book.",["Japanese","Fiction","Magical Realism","Contemporary"],"haruki-murakami"),

