mk("AUTHORS","Author","Ursula K. Le Guin","Wrote 'The Left Hand of Darkness' in 1969 — a sci-fi novel that treats gender as a social construct decades before that was mainstream. Her parents were anthropologists, and her fiction always reads like ethnography of imaginary cultures. Her Earthsea books proved fantasy could be literary before anyone else tried.","","A Wizard of Earthsea, first 3 chapters",25,"Read the opening. Ged, a boy with a gift for magic, goes to wizard school and in a fit of pride summons a shadow monster. The rest of the novel is the chase — but the shadow is hunting him too. Notice Le Guin's magic isn't a set of rules but a moral weight: every spell has a cost, and names are power.",["American","Fantasy","Science Fiction","20th Century"],"ursula-le-guin"),

